{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:48:26.113Z","ordinal":96,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a19b70-7336-77f2-a5a5-f8aefbea889b","turn_id":"01a19b70-7341-7e12-98d5-3e6b1c15e0f0","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"07378157df44b68a2b6c74bc26f69182_rs","summary_text":[],"raw_content":["The command is running in the background as a session. The instruction says \"沙箱后台进程会被回收，长任务必须用前台 exec 命令跑完再返回\". I used yield_time_ms which returned a session. Hmm, the tool returned a session ID. I need to poll it. Actually, the note says the session should be run in foreground — the exec_command tool with a session is effectively a foreground process attached to a PTY-ish stream; the risk described is about background processes (e.g. `&`). Since exec_command with yield returns a session I can poll, and the process is still running (not backgrounded with `&`), polling should be fine.\n\nBut the warning says \"沙箱后台进程会被回收\" — sandbox background processes get reaped. The exec session is managed by the harness, so it should persist. Let me poll it with write_stdin.\n\nLet me wait and poll."]},"started_at_ms":1793609303890,"completed_at_ms":1793609306113}}
